          {"key": "Other Pit", "line": {"v": "Trou", "t": "V"}} ] },
      "out": { "verdict": "thin", "word": null, "keys": [], "rivals": [] },
      "why": "the same text on four lines, two of which name the term: 2 against 2 is not a majority, so no stretch is confined to the term. (Two terms in the SAME keys, whose lines are all the block's, are the case of ambiguity: of_all/two-terms-the-same-block)" },
    { "id": "term_evidence/of/a-plural-is-another-word", "op": "of",
      "in": { "term": "Speed", "lines": [
